मण्डलम् पारम् ॥   ॰ paaram — THE CALLEE HALF of the cross-module pair

॰ THE ANSWER IS ४२, and it is `सेतुः.t1` that answers it: this module declares
॰ the routine and nothing calls it from here.
॰
॰ ANSWERED 2026-09-21T16:22Z, tree `2d116943`. This half compiles on its own —
॰ `t1_boot --object` reads `object: पारम् text 1877 object 960 records false`,
॰ which nothing had ever asked before — and it exports `॥ वैश्विकम्
॰ पारम्द्विगुणय ॥`, the exact symbol `सेतुः.t1`'s call names. The pair links and
॰ `yantra-run` halts `Finisher { value: 2765619, status: Some(42) }`. Withhold
॰ this object and the caller STOPS AT link with a refusal, so the ४२ above is
॰ this routine's and not the caller's.
॰
॰ WHY THIS PAIR IS NOT IN `spec/demo/`. The demonstration's third section runs
॰ EVERY `.t1` in that directory and compares what it answered with the
॰ `THE ANSWER IS` line in its own margin (`frontend/src/lib.rs:1115`), and
॰ `compile_and_run` (`:1079`) links ONE module object beside the startup. A
॰ program that spans two modules cannot run there — not because it is wrong,
॰ because that driver links one object. `t1_population.rs:100-114` also pins
॰ the six by name. So the pair lives here, is reached by `--compiler` and an
॰ explicit source list, and breaks nothing that walks `spec/demo/`.

सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः द्विगुणय आदाय संख्या ॱॱ न६४ ददाति न६४ आदि
    प्रत्यागमनम् संख्या योगः संख्या ।
इति
